course: dictionary
lesson: 2719
title: Context clues: dingo
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dingo is a kind of animal, and the words around it tell you what it is. «Dingoes are wild dogs that came to Australia with people thousands of years ago.» The clues wild dogs and Australia show you the dingo is a dog that lives in Australia.
explain: «They howl rather than bark» tells you how dingoes are different from pet dogs. Rather than means instead of, so a dingo makes a howling sound, not a barking one. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «A fence more than 5000 kilometres long keeps them away from sheep farms.» The words fence, keeps away and sheep farms are clues that dingoes can be a danger to sheep. If you do not know a word, read on and look for clues, and check a dictionary when the clues are not enough.
fact: A dingo is a wild dog of Australia, usually sandy-yellow in colour.
fact: Dingoes hunt alone or in packs.
fact: Dingoes howl rather than bark.
fact: Dingoes are a top predator, so campers are warned not to feed them.
fact: Dingoes came to Australia with people thousands of years ago.
exercise: What is a dingo? | A type of long fence | *A wild dog of Australia | A tall tree from the desert | A kind of sheep
exercise: «They howl rather than bark.» What does rather than mean here? | Even more than | Before | *Instead of | Along with
exercise: Why is a very long fence built in Australia? | To keep kangaroos in the desert | To hold back the sea | *To keep dingoes away from sheep | To stop people walking on the beach
test: Which colour is a dingo usually? | Snow-white | Bright blue | *Sandy-yellow | Jet-black
test: What should campers remember about dingoes? | Give them sweets to be friends | *Never feed them | Let them sleep in the tent | Always feed them scraps
exam: Dingoes hunt in which way? | Only by barking | Only in the sea | Only with humans | *Alone or in packs
